    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2VvsAv9bMnVw5hmscGggixs)_\n\n## What\nThe `M-x` text still glitched in Org after #152 and #154, and the cause was not found. As asked, `sp-posframe` is rewritten as a plain setup: `vertico-posframe` centred, 4 pixels of padding (border in the background colour), terminal fallback. That is the whole module.\n\nRemoved:\n- the nano-style prompt and the dotted line (`sp-posframe-divider-*`, `sp-posframe-nano-commands`),\n- the dimming (`sp-posframe-dim-*`),\n- the fixed width (`sp-posframe-width-fraction`) and the text size reset,\n- `sp-posframe-debug-minibuffer`.\n\nAlso removed: `sp-minibuffer` is no longer on `minibuffer-mode-hook` in `sp-fonts`, so the minibuffer text is at the `default` size (the function and `sp-minibuffer-face` stay). A larger font than the frame was sized for is a common cause of clipped text in a posframe. This also changes the size of the plain minibuffer.\n\nDocs: `sp-posframe.org` rewritten (with a section on what was removed), plus `dividers-and-lines.org`, `sp-fonts.org`, `main.org` and `CHANGELOG.org`.\n\n## Not tested\nNothing was run in Emacs (none in the container). If the glitch remains with this setup, it is outside this module; the doc lists where to look next (`popper`, other packages that change windows).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBs9srTW9kUiGXduSF)_",
